        "why": "The number of orbitals of a given type comes from the values m can take, which is 2l + 1. For p, l = 1 gives three values of m, and that is exactly why three p orbitals are drawn.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing m = 0, 1, 2 for a p orbital. The values run from −l to +l.",
          "Saying an s orbital has a nodal plane. For s, l = 0, so it has none."
